From e3bcc1f4c53b1cd71e440b41d98a75f42a6c11c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lwb6 <lwb.6@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:49:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] build: add a Windows build with stubbed media

Keep every product target and its link graph while removing FFmpeg and libcurl from the Windows
configuration, so a platform port can be built without a media toolchain. The stub translation
units keep the exact symbols and throw at runtime instead of returning partial data.

Link the CUDA runtime statically on Windows so a built tree needs no cudart DLL, compile utf8proc
as a static library (its header otherwise defaults to dllimport), and add the configure/build
scripts plus the portable CUDA 12.8 fetcher that the Windows recipe uses.
---
 CMakeLists.txt                                |  47 +++++---
 bench/CMakeLists.txt                          |   2 +-
 scripts/windows/build.cmd                     |  40 +++++++
 scripts/windows/configure.cmd                 |  65 ++++++++++
 scripts/windows/fetch_cuda_toolkit.py         | 113 ++++++++++++++++++
